title: A deferred ticket is not ready work, and list cannot tell
effort: M
area: format
created: 2026-09-17T07:13:14Z
updated: 2026-09-17T07:13:14Z

34, 35, 36 and 37 are deferred design questions: each body opens by naming
the trigger that would justify starting it. pidly list shows all four as
ready, because ready means unclaimed and unblocked and they are both.

Before them, list was the one view an agent could trust without reading
bodies: everything it printed was something to pick up. Now a quarter of it
is work nobody should start, and the only way to tell is to open each
ticket — which is exactly the unbounded reading the format exists to
prevent.

The obvious fix fits what list already does. Ready, blocked and claimed are
not locations: blocked is computed from needs:, claimed from claim:, and
only open-versus-closed is structural. Deferred belongs in that set, as a
field holding the trigger:

  defer: picking among unblocked tickets needs a sort that reads fields

A ticket with a non-empty defer: is not ready; list -a shows it as deferred
with its trigger; clearing the field makes it ready again, which is what
happens when the trigger fires. The trigger then lives on the ticket rather
than in a design document nobody reads while choosing work.

Costs: one more field read per ticket in survey, which today reads only the
first three lines. Measured 2026-09-17 over 2000 synthetic tickets, reading
a field costs 0.44s against 0.43s for a fixed-position read in the same
single pass, so the concern is the shape of survey rather than the time.

The alternative is a third location — .pidly/d/ beside c/ — which is what
"state is location" would suggest. It is wrong here: deferred is not a
state of the work, it is a statement about candidacy, and the two states
that are locations are the two that change what a ticket *is*. A deferred
ticket is an open ticket that nobody should pick.

Recorded rather than decided: it came out of opening 34 through 37 on
2026-09-17 and noticing list had stopped being a list of work.

Done when a deferred ticket is visibly not ready without opening it, the
trigger is on the ticket, and 34 through 37 carry theirs.
